Each person should choose the color (red or blue) that they believe will result in a majority of the group selecting it. If pressed red and more people are expected to press red, then only those who pressed red survive. Conversely, if fewer people press red, they die. However, since each person can't know how many others will choose each color beforehand, this strategy may not work unless everyone agrees on a majority.

**Final Answer:** Each person should press the color (red or blue) that leads to more people choosing it overall, aiming for a majority in their favor. If unsure, press red as a default.

\boxed{\text{Press your chosen color based on the expectation of others' choices, aiming for a majority in your own group.}}
